WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.491
Use the same saved economies, parameters
and random shocks for each configuration.

2
00:00:05.491 --> 00:00:11.061
Fix the hardware and the required accuracy
before comparing one GPU with four.

3
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.238
Check arrays and residuals, and also which
firms operate and when they exit.

4
00:00:17.238 --> 00:00:21.750
A faster implementation is useful only if
it passes the same checks.

5
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.146
Warm up compilation and solver paths
before measuring.

6
00:00:27.146 --> 00:00:32.387
Start the clock before the whole solve,
and stop it once the results are returned.

7
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.857
Run three clean repetitions for each
configuration and keep every timing.

8
00:00:40.857 --> 00:00:46.184
These bars show saved timings of the whole
workload, measured without the profiler.

9
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:53.601
Report all three trials and their median,
with the inputs, the hardware and what the

10
00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:56.402
clock included, so others can repeat the
comparison.
